  "title": "Pair failures that interact with higher layers are #P-hard when the edge is clean: a Brunnian rank lemma",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting homomorphisms from 3-manifold groups into finite solvable groups",
  "conclusion": "Gadget knots whose blocks return exactly to the meridian value make the count an edge-local integer partition function whose edge count is maximal on the diagonal, where the Borromean insertion is trivial, and strictly smaller across a pair-failing difference. So higher layers cannot cancel hardness, and with a character-0 refinement this decides 55 interacting census algebras.",
